# Trivy vulnerability suppressions.
# Each entry requires a justification consistent with the project's security posture.
# Review this file when upgrading base images or dependencies.

# CVE-2024-23342: ecdsa — Minerva timing attack on ECDSA keys
# Suppressed: transitive dep of python-jose; app uses HS256 (HMAC) JWTs exclusively,
# not EC keys. No fix available upstream. Consistent with pip-audit suppression.
CVE-2024-23342

# CVE-2025-69720: ncurses — buffer overflow in python:3.12-slim (debian 13.4)
# Suppressed: no fix available in debian 13.4. ncurses is not used by the application;
# it is present as an indirect OS dependency.
CVE-2025-69720

# CVE-2026-4878: libcap — privilege escalation via TOCTOU in cap_set_file()
# Suppressed: no fix available in debian 13.4. libcap is an indirect OS dep;
# the container runs as non-root (appuser) and does not call cap_set_file().
CVE-2026-4878

# CVE-2026-29111: systemd — arbitrary code execution via spurious IPC
# Suppressed: no fix available. systemd is an indirect OS dep in python:3.12-slim;
# it is not reachable from the application and the container runs as non-root (appuser).
CVE-2026-29111

# CVE-2026-4046: glibc — DoS via iconv() with specific character sets (libc-bin, libc6)
# Suppressed: fix_deferred in debian 13.4 — no patched version available.
# glibc iconv is not invoked by the application; present only as an OS base image dep.
CVE-2026-4046

# CVE-2026-40356: krb5 — DoS via integer underflow leading to out-of-bounds read (CWE-191)
# in MIT Kerberos 5 (libgssapi-krb5-2). Upstream fix available in krb5 >= 1.22.3; the
# container (debian 13.4, trixie) ships 1.21.3-5 with no patched debian package available yet.
# libgssapi-krb5-2 is an indirect OS dependency — not reachable from the application, which
# uses JWT/bcrypt authentication exclusively. Revisit when debian 13.4 packages krb5 >= 1.22.3.
CVE-2026-40356

# Frontend npm devDependency CVEs
# The following packages are transitive dependencies of build/test tooling
# (jest, playwright, next build) installed in the dev container. They are not
# in the HTTP request path. npm audit --audit-level=critical handles
# critical-severity npm CVEs at pre-commit time.

# CVE-2024-21538: cross-spawn — ReDoS via regex
CVE-2024-21538

# CVE-2025-64756: glob — command injection via malicious path
CVE-2025-64756

# CVE-2026-26996, CVE-2026-27903, CVE-2026-27904: minimatch — DoS variants
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# CVE-2026-23745, CVE-2026-23950, CVE-2026-24842, CVE-2026-26960,
# CVE-2026-29786, CVE-2026-31802: node-tar — path traversal / file overwrite variants
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802

# Perl CVEs in controlroom_backend — no fix available in debian trixie
# Perl is not used by the application (Python/FastAPI backend). The Dockerfile
# explicitly purges perl, perl-modules-5.40, and libperl5.40; perl-base may
# survive as an indirect OS dep but is not reachable from the application.
# Revisit when debian trixie ships patched perl 5.40 packages.

# CVE-2026-42496 (CRITICAL): Archive::Tar < 3.08 — symlink extraction attack
CVE-2026-42496

# CVE-2026-8376 (CRITICAL): Perl <= 5.43.10 — heap buffer overflow during compilation
CVE-2026-8376

# CVE-2026-42497 (HIGH): Archive::Tar < 3.08 — hardlink extraction attack
CVE-2026-42497

# CVE-2026-9538 (HIGH): Archive::Tar < 3.10 — memory exhaustion via crafted archive
CVE-2026-9538

# CVE-2026-48962 (HIGH): perl-IO-Compress — arbitrary code execution via attacker-controlled output glob
CVE-2026-48962
